!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 01: Basic D&D 2024 Beacon NPC Stats
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| This tutorial shows the simplest way to read common values from a D&D 2024
  --/| Beacon character sheet with ScriptCards.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a token that represents a D&D 2024 Beacon NPC.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. Compare the values on the output card with the character sheet.
  --/|
  --/| WHAT THIS TEACHES
  --/| A reference such as [*S:hp] reads a value from the source character.
  --/| The S means Source. The source character is set below with sourcetoken.
  --/|
  --/| Names such as hp, hp_max, npc_ac, strength, and strength_mod are direct
  --/| aliases. Direct aliases are the easiest way to read common sheet values.
  --/|
  --/| In .135, several familiar NPC compatibility values are reconstructed locally
  --/| from the active Beacon record graph. That includes formatted senses,
  --/| languages, defenses, and the flags that tell an existing ScriptCard whether
  --/| an NPC has saves, skills, or reactions to display.
  --/|
  --/| CURRENT AND MAXIMUM VALUES
  --/| On the D&D 2024 Beacon sheet, current HP and final maximum HP are exposed
  --/| as separate direct aliases:
  --/|
  --/| hp      = current Hit Points
  --/| hp_max  = final maximum Hit Points
  --/|
  --/| Beacon also has a separate structured "max tree" that can be requested
  --/| with ^ on a complete structured or typed lookup. That is a different idea
  --/| from the hp_max compatibility alias and is covered in Tutorial 02.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial only reads information. It does not change the character.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --/| Beacon support must be enabled when working with a Beacon sheet.
  --#beaconsheet|1

  --/| The selected token becomes the source token.
  --/| After this, [*S:...] references read from that token's character.
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}

  --/| A sheet value can be used anywhere a ScriptCards value is accepted.
  --#title|[*S:npc_name] - Basic Stats Tutorial

  --+|[c][b]Basic Information[/b][/c]

  --+Name|[*S:npc_name]
  --+Type|[*S:npc_type]
  --+Armor Class|[*S:npc_ac]

  --+|[c][b]Current and Maximum Hit Points[/b][/c]

  --/| These are two separate Beacon direct aliases.
  --+Current HP|[*S:hp]
  --+Maximum HP|[*S:hp_max]

  --+|[c][b]Other Basic Values[/b][/c]

  --+Speed|[*S:npc_speed]
  --+Challenge Rating|[*S:npc_challenge]
  --+Proficiency Bonus|[*S:pb]

  --+|[c][b]NPC Section Flags[/b][/c]

  --/| These compatibility flags are useful when deciding whether to show a
  --/| section in an NPC card. A value of 1 means at least one applicable entry
  --/| exists; 0 means none.
  --+Has Saving Throws|[*S:npc_saving_flag]
  --+Has Skills|[*S:npc_skills_flag]
  --+Has Reactions|[*S:npcreactionsflag]

  --+|[c][b]Ability Scores[/b][/c]

  --/| Ability scores and ability modifiers are separate direct aliases.
  --/| For example, strength is the score and strength_mod is the modifier.
  --+Strength|[*S:strength] ([*S:strength_mod])
  --+Dexterity|[*S:dexterity] ([*S:dexterity_mod])
  --+Constitution|[*S:constitution] ([*S:constitution_mod])
  --+Intelligence|[*S:intelligence] ([*S:intelligence_mod])
  --+Wisdom|[*S:wisdom] ([*S:wisdom_mod])
  --+Charisma|[*S:charisma] ([*S:charisma_mod])

  --+|[c][b]Other NPC Information[/b][/c]

  --/| Some direct aliases return formatted text rather than one number.
  --+Senses|[*S:npc_senses]
  --+Languages|[*S:npc_languages]
  --+Vulnerabilities|[*S:npc_vulnerabilities:::None]
  --+Resistances|[*S:npc_resistances:::None]
  --+Damage Immunities|[*S:npc_immunities:::None]
  --+Condition Immunities|[*S:npc_condition_immunities:::None]
}}
